// Settlane: milestone settlement of digital-service agreements (Fe 26.6.0, EVM).
//
// Modules (files in this directory):
//   types     storage types, the Clock effect, events.
//   rules     pure settlement rules. No effects: time arrives as an argument.
//   handlers  shared handler bodies (D-016). Both the production contract and the
//             dev ingot's test-clock shell call these, so the deadline-crossing
//             tests exercise the shipped code.
//   settlane  the message type and the production contract.
//
// Phase 3A implements creation, funding, evidence, review, `Claim` and the queries. Refund is
// not implemented yet. `Settlane` DECLARES the `Call` effect, so it can send ETH, but only the
// `Claim` arm lists it (the compiler rejects any arm that omits it, `8-0012`/`8-0036`; one that
// lists it read-only still compiles, FE_NOTES E7, so the lint rules E-CALL and E-BODY are the
// guard). Even `Claim` has exactly one way to send: the approved transfer in `claim_handler`
// (lint C-XFER, R-005 F-1).
